        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays aren't just fighting for positioning - they're clawing back from a two-game Mets split to prove they still belong in the AL East hunt. <strong>Last night's 9-3 rout of the Mets</strong> was the kind of offensive explosion that reminds fans this team can still light up the scoreboard when the pitching clicks, even if they sit at 41-46 and 11.5 games behind the division leader. The bullpen, which imploded in the 0-3 loss a day earlier, finally found its rhythm, and the lineup - led by hot hands in the middle innings - didn't let a single chance slip. With a one-game win streak now in place and the AL Central trailing just 2.5 points, the momentum is real, but the road remains steep. <strong>Next up: Saturday's 10:10 PM ET showdown at Seattle</strong>, where the Jays must turn another ALCS rematch into a regular-season win to keep their contender pulse alive.",
